---
title: Amaretto Sour
servings: 1
tags: [cocktail, amaretto]
source: Classic cocktail, number 11 on Drinks International's 2026 bestselling classics; method written for this repository
---

In a #cocktail shaker{} without ice, pour @amaretto{1.5%fl_oz}, @bourbon{0.75%fl_oz}, @lemon juice{1%fl_oz}, @simple syrup{1%tsp} and @egg white{0.5}. Shake hard for ~{10%seconds}, add ice, and shake again for ~{10%seconds}. Strain into a #rocks glass{}(with fresh ice). Garnish with a @lemon peel{1%twist} and a @cocktail cherry{1}.

> The bourbon is the modern fix that keeps it from being too sweet; leave it out for the older, sweeter drink.
